preConditionHook:
// EL: bigBar = false; for ii = 0 to window - 1: sum high - low over the
// lookback bars ending at ii + 1, divide by lookback, and set bigBar when
// high[ii] - low[ii] >= rangeMultiple * that mean.
// The benchmark EXCLUDES the bar being judged, so a huge bar cannot raise its
// own benchmark. The EL twin writes the mean as an inner for loop rather than
// Average(high - low, lookback)[ii + 1] because a function-history reference at
// a loop-variable offset is not a behaviour the register covers; the value is
// the same, since Average recomputes from scratch every bar (EL_Summation_Probe,
// 2,808/2,808) over a price expression with real history. Summed newest-first,
// EL's Summation order, and divided by the same (int) bound the loop uses.
// high - low, not TrueRange and not the WFSafe_ rolling accumulator: gaps are
// excluded, which is what separates this from BarRangeAboveAtrMultiple.
// Scratch locals persist across bars, so all three are reset before use.
bigBar = false;
for (int i = 0; i < (int)window; ++i) {
    rangeSum = 0.0;
    for (int j = 0; j < (int)lookback; ++j) {
        rangeSum = rangeSum + (high[i + 1 + j] - low[i + 1 + j]);
    }
    avgRange = rangeSum / (int)lookback;
    if (el_ge(high[i] - low[i], rangeMultiple * avgRange)) {
        bigBar = true;
    }
}
